A||N||12||MontanaFiero||3.4L Camaro Motor||||5||
Z||000000||MontanaFiero||02-28-2001||01:43 PM||||OK --<BR>I am supposed to be rebuilding my 2.8, but I ran across a <B>'93 Iron Head Camaro 3.4 Liter V6</B> with only 9,000 miles on it. It's been sitting on a shelf for several years. I understand the car was wrecked a month after it was bought new. It has no flywheel (so can I use the one from the 2.8?)  They want $1200 for it- am I paying too much?<P>Will my manifolds bolt up to those heads?  If not, shouldn't I be able to retrofit the camaro computer into my Fiero's system? (I <I>can</I> wire). <P>------------------<BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- <I>project</I> &lt;&lt;||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfixit58||02-28-2001||03:16 PM||||$1200 sounds little too much if you were in Florida but Montana! I dunno. If the motor has been sitting for eight years, you'd think he would be ready to get rid of it. Try these links: <A HREF="http://www.copartfinder.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.copartfinder.com/</A>  <A HREF="http://www.tacreationsusa.com/v6.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tacreationsusa.com/v6.htm</A> <P>Find out from them and how much to ship and see if your guy is in the ball park. If they are lower, make him a simular offer or maybe a few $$$ less. Ask him how much it's gonna cost him to leave it sit on the shelf for another eight years. After all, it's not like it's a Corvette motor!<P>For the conversion, remember to factor in the cost to re-drill the starter holes to the other side and to modify the bracket (see Ed Parks article: <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34</A>  )<P>Good Luck,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||87GTZ34||03-01-2001||05:40 PM||||Sounds fishy to me.  That motor should not have been on the shelf long with only 9K mi on it.  Tell them you want to hear it run before you plunk any money down.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||03-01-2001||06:06 PM||||Unless you have an 88 2.8 you will need the flywheel. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||rockcrawl||03-01-2001||07:19 PM||||If it was wrecked when it was only a month old, how did it get 9000 miles on it? That's almost a years worth of driving for most people. Sounds fishy.||||reg||1
Z||000005||MontanaFiero||03-02-2001||01:56 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rockcrawl:<BR><B>If it was wrecked when it was only a month old, how did it get 9000 miles on it? That's almost a years worth of driving for most people. Sounds fishy.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well <I>I</I> said a month, but I think his exact words were "shortly after buying it new".<P>I don't know... up here there just doesn't seem to be much demand for those motors, I guess. It does bother me that it has been on the shelf that long-- I'm sure It will need new seals.<p>[This message has been edited by MontanaFiero (edited 03-02-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||ironhedno3||03-02-2001||07:35 AM||||hi my name is keith..give me a call if ya wanna a reman 3.4..call grooms engines at 1-800-950-7711..ask for keith..you can reach me mon-fri 8-4:30 central time<p>[This message has been edited by ironhedno3 (edited 03-02-2001).]||||reg||6
